Date: Wed, 17 Mar 93 11:50:12 CST
From: Marlin Johnson <bsc835!mjohnson@uunet.UU.NET>
Subject: META: Extropianism lost/paying for the priviledge

As Tim May was saying not so long ago:

 TM> I enjoy these speculations about (somehow) creating a kind of
 TM> "market" for posting privileges...I just can't any plausible way to
 TM> do it.  Paying for posts was once discussed--that would just stop
 TM> some of us from sharing our contributions with the list (is this
 TM> what you want?).

Have you considered coupling "paying for posts" with allowing people
to reward "worthwhile" posts?  Suppose a price per post is set at 5
exidits (extropian institute credits?) and each person upon
subscribing to the list is granted 100 exidits, enough for twenty
posts, and an account number in the ExI Bank.  Debits for posting
could be handled automatically.  And folks who wished to reward the
poster could send an e-mail to the ExI Bank authorizing a transfer
of funds to an account number which the poster could display in his
or her .sig.

There are lots of details that could be diddled one way or the other
to fine tune the cash flow, like do funds in the bank gain interest
over time (to encourage hording) or maybe they start losing interest
after sitting still for a time (to encourage banking activity)?
Perhaps the bank pays each list member a set amount per day or week
simply for being there.

Some combination of these factors could be used to prevent the funds
from pooling in the pockets of a few and allow newbies, like myself
:-) to play along as well, such as a negitive interest debited daily
then redispersed by the bank on a weekly basis.

Anyway, I'm sure there are folks around here able to cobble the
details of such a thing better than I, but I did want to get down
enough of the idea to see if anyone else found it interesting.


