Agreement?!  But I thought we were scheduled for a duel!  You had said:

>Shhee-it, Tom, I'm a callin' ya out! We're a gonna have us a genu-ine
>shootout at the Extropian Corral!

I was looking forward to firing my most lethal logical analyses at you
("Sloppy argument!"  "Circular reasoning!") and you were going to respond
with sharply-worded epistemological verdicts ("Unfounded belief!"  "Druidic
claptrap!").  

Well, in the interest of keeping a lively conflict chugging along, I'm
going to present a moving target.  Now, instead of saying that Robin's
Polite Society is marred by the inability to effectively impose costs on
lurkers, I am going to suggest that a revision might allow it to do so
after all.  What sort of revision?  Dumping tons 'o email into the lurkers'
addresses if they are shot.  

Why should lurkers care about getting overloaded in email?  Because, if
done properly, it will interfere with their ability to lurk.  This would
require that 1) we know the lurkers' real addresses, and that 2) we
disguise bogus email so that it is indistinguishable from the real stuff,
forcing the errant lurker to waste lots of time on decoys before finding
the meaty email.

Note that while the Polite Society quite rightly targets the posting rights
of those who *aren't* lurkers, this email dumping techinque would probably
work just as well on them.  Everybody, I'd guess, likes to read email.

