Hmm.. both T.M.s (heh - has anyone ever seen them in the same room?),
each a frequent poster, think my proposed society is unfair to
frequent posters, even in a netwide context.  As a hacker, I don't say
"fatal error" I say "bug"; so let me keep hacking the organizational
design to reduce apparent problems.

First, for the imagined "feuding" problem of two parties shooting back
and forth again and again, I propose only allowing each person to shot
each other person once.  Feuds now require clans, and the # hits
statistic now measures how many people ever thought you were impolite.
# shots says how many people you ever thought were impolite.

To improve fairness to frequent posters, we need only package a
posting requirement in with the procedure for shooting.  Let us say
that the shot itself must be posted in the same context where the
accused impolite post was.  In addition we can say that the shooter
must show that they can do better.  The shooter must submit a copy of
a post that shooter made, again in the same context, which was made
*after* the rude post and before the shot, and which the shooter
claims deals with a similar social situation but is more polite.
